<title>HUNGARY: MOL to raise wages by 17 percent in 1997.</title>
<headline>MOL to raise wages by 17 percent in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian oil and gas company MOL Rt said on Friday it will raise base wages by an average 17 percent in 1997 as a result of an agreement with trade unions.</p>
<p>The wage rise will be implemented on May 1 retroactive to January 1, MOL said in a statement, published in the official bourse gazette.</p>
<p>MOL and the trade unions also agreed to provide employees with a one-off share package worth the half of average base wages, it said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
